  "levels": [
    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "What is a share?",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "What is a share?"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-co-to-jest-akcja.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **share** is a stake in a company. By buying even one, you become a **co-owner** of the company and have a right to part of its profits."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You make money in two ways:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Price growth** – the company grows and someone buys your stake for more",
                "**Dividend** – the company shares its profit with you"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "What is a dividend?",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "What is a dividend?"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-co-to-jest-dywidenda.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **dividend** is the part of the profit a company pays out to shareholders, most often in cash. It's a reward for trusting the company with your capital."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Young, fast-growing companies** – usually invest all their profit in growth",
                "**Mature, stable companies** – pay out regularly, e.g. once a year or every quarter"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "The company decides on the payout – a dividend is **not guaranteed**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "What is an ETF?",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "What is an ETF?"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-co-to-jest-etf-2.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "An **ETF** (Exchange-Traded Fund) is a fund listed on the stock exchange – a ready-made **basket** of dozens or even thousands of stocks or bonds. One unit is a piece of every company inside."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**It tracks an index**, e.g. the S&P 500 or MSCI World",
                "**It diversifies** your money straight away",
                "**It has low fees** compared with traditional funds"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "An ETF's value still **moves up and down with the market**."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/download.jpg",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 220,
              "caption": ""
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
