    {
      "id": "l4",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "What is a bond?",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "What is a bond?"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/4-co-to-jest-obligacja.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A **bond** is a loan: you lend money to a state, a local government or a company. You're not a co-owner, but a **creditor**."
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Interest (coupon)** – your payment for the loan",
                "**Maturity date** – the day you get the whole amount back"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Bonds are usually **safer and more predictable** than stocks – but only as safe as the issuer is solvent."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
